---
description: Rules for fetching data in React components
globs: astro-app/src/components/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---
- Use the existing React Query nanostores store from here [query.ts](mdc:astro-app/src/stores/query.ts)
- Import `queryClient` from `@/stores/query` and use `useStore(queryClient)` to get the QueryClient instance
- Pass the QueryClient instance as the second parameter to React Query hooks: `useQuery({...}, client)` or `useMutation({...}, client)`
- The QueryClient instance can be named `client` or `$queryClient` (following nanostores convention)
- Every React query should call an Astro Action
- Astro Actions are defined in `astro-app/src/actions/index.ts` and exported as the `server` object
- Astro Actions are accessed by importing `actions` from `astro:actions` and using `actions.*()` (e.g., `actions.picks.submitPick()`, `actions.users.login()`, `actions.reactions.addReaction()`)
- Actions use `defineAction` with `accept: 'json'` or `accept: 'form'` depending on the use case
- Gracefully handle errors in React components when calling actions (check for `error` property in response)
- Actions should throw `ActionError` class (from `astro:actions`) when errors occur that should be visible to the client
- Use `useQuery` for fetching data and `useMutation` for mutations
- Always provide proper query keys for cache management
